course: dictionary
lesson: 14226
title: Napping: sleeping, and caught napping
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Napping means sleeping for a short time, especially during the day. «The baby is napping, so please speak quietly.» The clues are the cot and the request for quiet, so napping means asleep for a while.
explain: Caught napping is a phrase with a second meaning. It is informal, so you hear it in everyday talk and sport. «The keeper was caught napping, and the ball rolled into the net.» Here it means not paying attention or not ready, not actually asleep.
explain: Nap is the base word. You can say «Grandad had a nap after lunch», so a nap is also a noun for a short sleep. Ask yourself: is someone sleeping, or is someone unprepared? The sentence tells you which.
fact: Napping means sleeping for a short time, especially during the day.
fact: The forms are nap, naps, napped and napping. A nap is a short sleep.
fact: «Caught napping» means caught not paying attention or not ready.
fact: Many animals nap during the day.
fact: Caught napping is informal, so use it in chatty speech, not in formal writing.
exercise: «The baby is napping, so let's speak quietly.» What does napping mean here? | Eating a big meal | Running very fast | *Sleeping for a short time | Shouting loudly
exercise: «The keeper was caught napping and the ball went in.» What does caught napping mean? | Fast asleep in bed all night | Caught in a net | *Not ready or not paying attention | Sleeping on the bus
exercise: Which word is a noun for a short sleep? | *a nap | napping | napped | naps the baby
test: «Yesterday she napped for an hour after school.» What does napped mean? | *Slept for a short time | Ran home quickly | Sang a song | Forgot her homework
test: «The guard was caught napping, and the thief walked straight past.» What does caught napping suggest? | Fast asleep in bed for the night | Ready for a race | *Not paying attention | Hiding in a box
exam: Which sentence uses napping to mean sleeping for a short time? | The team was caught napping at kick-off. | She is napping her way to the top of the class. | *Grandad is napping in his chair after lunch.
